Drop resolved dynamic derivations from pending and keep graphing.

Nix announces dynamic-derivation resolution as a BuildWaiting activity
carrying `resolved derivation: '<old>.drv' -> '<new>.drv'` as its text
(see DerivationResolutionGoal::resolveDerivation in nix).

The unresolved derivation entered pending via the plan listing, but only
the resolved one ever runs (showing up via its own Build activity).
Moreover the resolved .drv file often lives only on a remote builder, so
nom can not read links for it: without handling, the unresolved entry
sits in pending forever and the resolved one renders as a disconnected
root, i.e. the graph goes flat.

On that notice, retire the old node and let the new one take over its
graph position: dependents are rewired from old to new, and when the new
node has no links of its own (its file could not be read) it inherits
the old node's inputs. A planned node additionally shows as completed
for a few seconds so the handoff is perceptible instead of instant.
Retired ids stay remembered so a late plan listing can not resurrect
them, and as provenance for the `resolved from` row annotation and the
resolved counter in the summary bar. Summaries follow through the
existing propagation (the old footprint leaves with the pending state,
the new one is inserted under the new parents; sets make this idempotent
and later transitions converge deterministically).

